[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports about wrong dates and marked them known. Read
by tenant and booking form, not by intake tag, they are not one bug.

<Callout>
Not one issue. #4471 fits one of the two problems. The other had no ticket of its own.
</Callout>

## How we counted

Each report is placed by its tenant: the locale it writes dates in and the booking form it
runs. The intake tag is a guess made from the reporter's browser, and it is wrong for dozens of
reports. The export also repeats some rows, so we count each report id once.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

1. **The shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant that writes the day first sees
   its dates flip. This is the problem #4471 describes. It is the large majority of the reports.
   The desk read a few of them as a one-day move (see the note under the table); they are filed
   here by tenant. **Fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
2. **The booking-v3 form tells day-first tenants to type `MM/DD/YYYY`.** People type what the
   hint says and the form reads it their way. This is a different bug: fixing the parser does
   not fix it. Three tenants run this form. It was merged into #4471 by mistake.
   **Won't fix:** the booking-v3 form is retired.

Each problem now has its own ticket in the
[#4471 follow-up repo](https://github.com/sftoolboxdev/what-it-shows-4471/issues), with its
report count.

## Lessons

- A big ticket is mostly one bug reported many times, until it is not. Check the cause before
  you merge, not only the subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges
  on subject alone).
- Do not trust the intake tag. Look up the tenant.

